A||||6||Alex2004||Are there  85 MPH backlit gauges?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||03-13-2001||02:35 PM||||I was wondering because mine has the reflection gauages and I want to replace them with backlit, i have an 84 se w/ a 4 cyl.  And how hard would it be to set the tach if i got some backlit gauges?  Oh, mine has the volt meter, and if i got an instrument cluster that has the oil pressure meter, would it read the oil pressure or read the voltage and jsut show it as the oil pressure?  Let me know!...  Thanks!<P>Alex...  <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||03-13-2001||02:40 PM||||Alex--<BR>You'd have to buy the whole cluster, including the auxiliary gauge pod. And yes, my SE is an early '86 and it has backlit 85 MPH gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||03-13-2001||07:01 PM||||85GT had backlit speedo/tach. no aux cluster required.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||03-14-2001||03:16 PM||||'85 GT did NOT have backlit gauges.  Same stupid reflectorized ones as on the other '85s and the '84s.  Only difference was the tach mounted gauge.  Volts for '84s & oil press for the '85s.<P>By the way, I'm working on my 2nd '85 GT and have swapped out both sets of gauges for backlit 120mph gauges out of an '87 GT.||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||03-14-2001||08:50 PM||||Monkeyman, you're right. I went to my parents house to look at my coupe( has 85 GT cluster) and they're not backlit.Sorry, thought they were. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-16-2001||10:37 AM||||I wish they did have backlit gauges.  Then I wouldn't have had the desire to spend my money on a set.  I didn't care about the 120 mph speedo (where the heck are you gonna go 120 mph anyhow?), I just wanted the better visibility.||||reg||1
